@startuml EcuKnockOut_Sequence

title ECU Knock-Out Timer Management

participant "OPMM" as OPMM
participant "ARA_S2S" as ARA_S2S
participant "ARA_PER(KVS)" as KVS
participant "rbdm" as rbdm
participant "ASW" as ASW

== POST-RUN State Reached ==

OPMM -> ARA_S2S: RBX_OPMM_MODE_RESPONSE_POST_RUN_STATE_REACHED

OPMM -> KVS: rbx_opmm_ECUKnockout_Write_To_Kvs
KVS -> OPMM: rbx_opmm_ECUKnockoutTimer_Read_From_Kvs

OPMM -> OPMM: Knockout timer Running

rbdm -> OPMM: KnockoutTestMode

note over OPMM
  OPMM Switch To RunState 
  When Veto Active
end note

opt KL15_ON
  note over OPMM
    OPMM in VETO State
    (VETO Timer: 120 seconds)
  end note
end

OPMM -> ARA_S2S: OperatingModesKeepAliveRequests_DRB
ARA_S2S -> OPMM: OperatingModeRequest_PowerBlade-RunState

note over OPMM
  Veto Timer Expired (120 Sec)
  Proceed with Shutdown
end note

== Knock-Out Timer Running ==

rbdm -> OPMM: KnockoutTestMode

note over OPMM
  OPMM Switch To RunState When
  KnockOut Timer is Running
end note

opt KL15_ON
  note over OPMM
    KL15 ON signal detected
    Return to RUN state
  end note
end

OPMM -> ARA_S2S: OperatingModesKeepAliveRequests_DRB
ARA_S2S -> OPMM: OperatingModeRequest_PowerBlade-RunState

note over OPMM
  OPMM Switch To RunState When
  KnockOut Timer is Running
end note

== Knock-Out Timer Expired ==

note over OPMM
  Continue With KnockOut Timer
end note

OPMM -> OPMM: KnockOut Timer Timeout

note over OPMM
  Knockout Timer Expired
end note

note over OPMM
  Increment the counter by 1
  and Store it in ARA_PER Kvs
end note

OPMM -> KVS: WriteKvs

note over OPMM
  OPMM Proceed for Safe Shutdown
end note

note right of OPMM
  **ECU Knock-Out Timer Flow:**
  
  1. POST-RUN State:
     - VETO Timer: 120 seconds
     - If KL15 ON → Return to RUN
     - If Timer Expires → Proceed to Shutdown
  
  2. Knock-Out Timer:
     - Runs after VETO expiration
     - Can be interrupted by KL15 ON
     - Timeout → Increment counter in KVS
  
  3. Counter Management:
     - Counter stored persistently in KVS
     - Incremented on each shutdown attempt
     - Used for ECU health monitoring
  
  4. Safe Shutdown:
     - After counter update
     - OPMM proceeds with graceful shutdown
end note

@enduml
